(Bug #59 over a map. A map's values are runtime-tagged the way a mixed
 list's slots are (LANGUAGE.md:2348-2350 - "the value carries its runtime
 tag, so a text prints as text and a number as a number"), so a `treating`
 clause walking them must keep each tag too.)

a map called person is {"name": "Ada", "age": 36}.
print each detail from person's values treating "Ada" as "Grace".
print each detail from person's values treating 36 as 37.
